      "content": "It is completely understandable that this feels relentless and exhausting, especially when the public perception feels so intense. Shifting the focus from the external view to your own internal process might offer a small anchor. Focus on finding one small, private act of self-care each day, something that quietly affirms your own value independent of others' judgments. Healing from a massive loss is not a quick recovery, but rather a slow, determined reconstruction from the inside out.",
      "source": "target",
